{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1 complete) — confirmed root cause, with the discriminating experiments\n\n### The mechanism, in two parts\n\n**(1) The budget now sits inside the band of legitimate test costs.** Commit `6a5c88027c5`\n(story `bold-abeyant-indri`) lowered the per-test hang budget 300 s -> 20 s at\n`pyproject.toml:650`, `_build-and-test.yml:662` and `:677`. `git blame -w -C -M` on all three\nlines returns `6a5c88027c59` and nothing else; its trailer is `rebar-ticket: 73b8-2d79-3046-44ce`.\n\nThe direct PARENT commit `4d6c1cc835e` — same day, same runner class, same\n`-n 4 --dist worksteal --cov=rebar`, still on `--timeout=300` — passed clean\n(run 32581500417 / job 97051623657: `16182 passed, 66 skipped in 906.38s`, zero crashes) and\nits own `--durations=25` block reports fourteen tests between **18.71 s and 29.93 s of `call`\ntime**, headed by 29.93 s / 28.72 s / 22.97 s / 22.63 s / 22.46 s / 22.44 s / 21.63 s. That list\nIS the crash list. So the evidence refuting \"20 s is measured, not guessed: the default tier\nruns clean at it\" was already in CI at the moment the change landed. `timeout_func_only = true`\ncannot rescue it: those are `call` times — the test body is the whole-tree scan.\n\nThe story's own measurement (\"the whole unit tier runs clean at `--timeout=20`, 5097 passed\") was\na LOCAL unit-tier run — no `--cov=rebar`, no `tests/scripts`, faster cores. The gating\n`ubuntu-latest, py3.13` leg is the only one that adds coverage, and it is the only leg that reds.\n\n**(2) `timeout_method = \"thread\"` expresses an expiry as a process kill, not as a verdict.**\n`pytest_timeout.py:542` (`timeout_timer`) calls `os._exit(1)` from the watchdog thread, so the\nxdist worker dies outright. Only the `signal` method reports `Failed: Timeout`, via\n`pytest.fail()` at `pytest_timeout.py:502`. **A budget expiry inside an xdist worker can\ntherefore NEVER print `Failed: Timeout`** — it prints `[gwN] node down: Not properly terminated`\nfollowed by `worker 'gwN' crashed while running '<test>'`.\n\nThis resolves the tension the report flagged: the zero `Failed: Timeout` count is a *prediction*\nof the mechanism, not evidence against it. Bug `albinic-agrologic-dolphin` (0078-fa3e-05d1-4e12)\nindependently proved the same mechanism last fortnight, and — pointedly — used\n`--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` as its deliberate crash-INDUCING amplifier to reproduce a\n300 s-budget bug. Story 73b8 then shipped that exact value as the production budget.\n\n### Discriminating experiments (local, worktree off 6a5c88027c5, macOS py3.12)\n\nA probe test with a 25 s body, run under `-n 2 --dist worksteal`:\n\n    ARM A  repo ini as shipped (timeout=20, thread)\n           -> [gw0] node down: Not properly terminated\n              worker 'gw0' crashed while running '<probe>'\n              zero `Failed: Timeout`                      == the CI signature, byte-identical\n    ARM B  same 20 s budget, --timeout-method=signal\n           -> E  Failed: Timeout (>20.0s) from pytest-timeout.\n              1 failed, 1 passed in 20.87s                 worker SURVIVES, clean verdict\n    ARM C  pre-73b8 budget, --timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread\n           -> 2 passed in 25.88s\n\nArm B isolates the METHOD as what converts a timeout into a worker crash (killing \"it is not the\ntimeout, it is something else\"). Arm C isolates the BUDGET as what makes it fire at all (killing\n\"the thread method was always broken\"). Together they leave only: over-tight budget + thread\nmethod = worker crash with no timeout verdict.\n\nSupporting measurement: `--cov=rebar` alone is a ~2x multiplier on these tests locally\n(`test_safe_boundary_is_not_unwrapped_in_repository_tests` 2.91 s -> 6.02 s;\n`test_gate_reports_no_findings_for_owned_files` 2.01 s -> 4.23 s). The runner's slower cores\nunder 4-way saturation supply the rest of the gap to 20 s.\n\n### Why it reads as flakiness rather than a hard failure\n\nThe budget lands *inside* the cost band, not below it, so which tests die depends on which\nmarginal test `--dist worksteal` hands to a loaded worker. The crashing set drifts between runs\n(`test_reconciler_jira_seam_clean_heldout` in job 97060825782,\n`test_residual_drain_seam_clean_heldout` in job 97056277838). And it is self-amplifying: eleven\nworker restarts re-pay process + coverage startup, so the suite takes 1057-1077 s instead of\n906 s and the SURVIVING scanners are pushed from ~16 s to 19.0-19.95 s — hard against the wall.\nEach crash makes the next more likely.\n\n### Pristine main IS affected; change 2098 / story 3436 is NOT implicated\n\nBoth failing runs carry headSha `6a5c88027c59d3e24d3e4269838fb3c591a64240`, which is pristine\n`origin/main` — no change in flight. Gerrit 2098's revision file list is\n`src/rebar/_commands/compact_{txn,rebuild,plan,recovery,trigger}.py`, `compact.py`,\n`tests/unit/commands/test_compact_plan.py`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_compact_negative.py`\n— none of the eleven crashing tests, and neither `pyproject.toml` nor `_build-and-test.yml`.\nMain itself is broken for every change; 2098 is collateral.\n\n### Defect legitimacy: `defect` (regression)\n\nCited authorities: (a) story 73b8's own commit-message claim that the tier \"runs clean at\" 20 s,\nfalsified by the parent commit's own CI durations; (b) bug `balsamy-eloquent-iggypops`\n(89d5-61da-b621-47f8), which established this guard and sized it at 300 s because \"300 s dwarfs\nthe slowest legitimate test\"; (c) bug `albinic-agrologic-dolphin`, whose RCA fixes the meaning of\nthis exact crash signature; (d) the project's landing rule that a change needs `Verified +1`.\n\n### Attribution\n\n`caused_by` -> **73b8-2d79-3046-44ce** (`bold-abeyant-indri`), introducing commit `6a5c88027c5`.\nClean regression, not an unmet obligation: the implicated lines were CREATED by that commit\n(blame returns only it), and the date test agrees — the parent commit ran the same tests clean at\n906 s with zero crashes. The link is recorded, and will be passed explicitly as `--caused-by` on\nthe close so blame auto-derivation cannot add a competing guessed edge.\n\n### Sibling sweep\n\nAll `--timeout=` lanes across `.github/workflows/` and the `Makefile`: the two lanes at 20 are\nthe ONLY ones below 300. The other eleven are 300 / 600 / 900 / 1800 / 3600 — separately\ncalibrated and all comfortably clear of the 29.93 s worst case. No construct siblings. Parity\ncensus on \"where is the per-test budget set\": local `pytest` + `make test` (the ini — covered by\nthe fix), the two shared CI lanes (fixed), the eleven other CI lanes (already >= 300). No MISSING\nslot."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787419248590104001,"uuid":"73261eb5-2ee3-450a-91a9-ff90db08656e"}